  "confirmed": [
    "All supplied preview, source, reference and diff pins match.",
    "R2248 explicitly allows Markdown as a value Format, separates direct-value constraints from occurrence/value counts, and does not generalize empty brackets.",
    "INSTANCE_OF keeps corresponding Property schema identity, data bearer and no independent Carrier; HAS_INSTANCE is a reverse name for one canonical fact, without inferred permissions.",
    "The generic Relation Declaration signature and inline existing-instance example remain distinct; typed union is one domain and no literal becomes a Node or instance is created."
  ],
  "limits": "Prospective previews only. Coordinated metadata, inverse migration and source adoption remain separate; no native/source/code/tests/Git changes.",
  "resolved_findings": [
    {
      "packet": "brackets",
      "issue": "General square-bracket explanation covers value Formats and conditions but omits the established nested Property-name selector contexts p.*[name format] and p.**[name format].",
      "fix": "Distinguish name-selector bracket use from direct-value Format without creating a general meaning for empty brackets."
    },
    {
      "packet": "model-reference",
      "issue": "The new Rule has no brief Semantics section and no explicit IF example of a bare Model entity and a selected instance; prose already limits mixed-domain Relations to admitted endpoint domains.",
      "fix": "Add concise Semantics and, if requested example is intended as normative illustration, show an IF example under an explicitly admitted Relation domain without granting new permission."
    }
  ],
  "resolution": "R2248 now identifies immediate and recursive Property-name selection separately; Model-reference includes concise Semantics and admitted INSTANCE_OF example. No IF example is required by latest instruction.",
